<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Side-by-side ("fusion") manifest embedded into notifyd.exe by build.rs.

  This is the half of the sparse-package story that is easy to miss, and missing
  it fails in the worst possible way: `Add-AppxPackage -ExternalLocation`
  succeeds, the package shows up in `Get-AppxPackage`, and the process still has
  NO identity at runtime. The exe has to point back at the package as well; the
  registration alone is not enough.

  Every attribute below must match dotfiles\notifyd-package\AppxManifest.xml:
    packageName   == Identity/@Name
    publisher     == Identity/@Publisher
    applicationId == Applications/Application/@Id
  A mismatch is reported as 0x80073D54, if it is reported at all.

  No trustInfo here on purpose: link.exe writes one for us (/MANIFESTUAC defaults
  to asInvoker), and two of them in one merged manifest is an error. asInvoker is
  what we want anyway. notifyd must never run elevated: Windows refuses to
  deliver COM callbacks into a high integrity level, so an elevated notifyd gets
  RPC_S_CALL_FAILED (0x800706BE) from the NotificationChanged subscription and
  silently degrades to polling only.
-->
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
  <assemblyIdentity version="1.0.0.0" name="Rice.Notifyd.notifyd" type="win32" />
  <msix xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:msix.v1"
        publisher="CN=RiceDotfiles"
        packageName="Rice.Notifyd"
        applicationId="notifyd" />
</assembly>
